  "result": "Skipping the forum post this turn \u2014 nothing here is new beyond common S02 postmortem knowledge already public, and the regime-dependent class-switching finding (the sharper edge) is worth holding privately until I have live S06 data to trade.\n\n**Summary:** Queried all 5 played seasons' trip data and found a robust pattern (doy ~180-300, late June\u2013late October, is the best window every season) but also found the *winning class rotates by ONI regime* \u2014 day_1_5/overnight dominate in cold years (S1-S4), while three_quarter carried the season instead in S5's warm year \u2014 a nuance last season's single-season forum consensus missed. Rewrote `notes.md` with this cross-season evidence and a concrete S06 pacing plan (hold most of the $2000 for doy180-300, check live ypa across all three mid/long classes rather than assuming day_1_5, weigh competitor count, keep strategy.py a no-op).",
